gdb/cris: skip missing special registers when single-stepping

CRIS has no hardware single-step, so gdb computes the next PC itself
in find_step_target.  That function reads all sixteen special registers,
but CRISv10 lacks P2, P3 and P6 (size 0, cris_cannot_fetch_register
rejects them), so every stepi and every resume from a breakpoint on a
v10 target failed with "Register 18 is not available".  Leave the
missing registers at zero instead.

Tested against qemu-system-cris (ETRAX 100LX, Linux 4.9).

--- a/gdb/cris-tdep.c	2026-10-24 01:40:47.252158752 +0200
+++ b/gdb/cris-tdep.c	2026-10-24 01:40:47.411162627 +0200
@@ -1972,8 +1972,12 @@
   offset = NUM_GENREGS;
   for (i = 0; i < NUM_SPECREGS; i++)
     {
-      inst_env->preg[i] = 
-	(unsigned long) regcache_raw_get_unsigned (regcache, offset + i);
+      /* Skip the special registers this CRIS version lacks.  */
+      if (cris_register_size (gdbarch, offset + i) == 0)
+	inst_env->preg[i] = 0;
+      else
+	inst_env->preg[i] =
+	  (unsigned long) regcache_raw_get_unsigned (regcache, offset + i);
     }
   inst_env->branch_found = 0;
   inst_env->slot_needed = 0;
